 "note": "Team-name normalization across the three bulk sources: cfbfastR-data schedules (ESPN naming, 2001-2025), jhowell.net historical scores (1990-2000), and collegepollarchive AP polls (1990-2025). Every join in scripts/build-candidates.mjs goes through this file. Lookup is on a loose slug (lowercased, '&' -> 'and', all other non-alphanumerics dropped), so casing, punctuation and spacing variants need no entry -- only genuinely different strings do. 'canonical' maps the canonical key to the display name; 'aliases' maps a source string to a canonical key. A source name that resolves to nothing is reported by build-candidates.mjs rather than silently dropped. Since 2026-09-29 'canonical' holds every team Howell counts as major in any season (byconf.htm), so the 1936-1977 polls and schedules join on the same keys. A non-major (a wartime service team the AP ranked) keeps Howell's x:<slug> id; an alias whose value is an x: id maps another source's spelling onto it.",
